{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1366, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nA positive integer not less than 10 whose top digit (the most significant digit) in decimal representation is strictly larger than every other digit in that number is called a Snake number.\nFor example, 31 and 201 are Snake numbers, but 35 and 202 are not.\nFind how many Snake numbers exist between L and R, inclusive.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nL R\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 10 \\leq L \\leq R \\leq 10^{18}\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n97 210\n\nSample Output 1\n\n6\n\nThe Snake numbers between 97 and 210, inclusive, are 97, 98, 100, 200, 201, and 210: there are six.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n1000 9999\n\nSample Output 2\n\n2025\n\nSample Input 3\n\n252509054433933519 760713016476190692\n\nSample Output 3\n\n221852052834757\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1401, "char_start": 1378, "quote": "Input:\n97 210\nOutput:\n6", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1442, "char_start": 1413, "quote": "Input:\n1000 9999\nOutput:\n2025", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1522, "char_start": 1454, "quote": "Input:\n252509054433933519 760713016476190692\nOutput:\n221852052834757", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "6337158875eaf2ed531caf8b2fcf5ec244e69bc6b1a3ad385c42fef8d8cedaff", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "9d2e50bba048b517e2e4896873e63e37bd6fa4ddb829539894000f2fd6600811", "seq": 2}
